{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/367347-single-pantheon-games","id":367347,"title":"Single Pantheon games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-12T07:45:41-08:00","id":367347,"title":"Single Pantheon games","content":"I just ended a game I had been running since the books came out (this game met rarely). In the post-game discussion, several players asked about running a new Scion game using only a single Pantheon (no other gods exist). While I could probably run a Dodekatheon game in my sleep, I keep looking at the Pesedjet or the Celestial Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else run a single-Pantheon game successfully?<br /> Does anyone have handy links/resources (outside of pantheon.org) for the Egyptian or Chinese myths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T15:44:53-08:00","id":367887,"title":"","content":"Ran a game of only Aesir and another of just Amatsukami. I didn't have any real problems with them. I would suggest that you get the players familiar with the pantheon.Almost everyone in the group was fairly familiar with Norse mythology.but were fairly unfamiliar with Japanese mythology. It took a while to get into the groove of playing Amatsukami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:12:07-08:00","id":369293,"title":"","content":"My initial thought is to run a game where magic has just re-entered the world due to the Titans breaking free. Fate, as is it wont, has caused descendants of the long-dead gods to find relics that will awaken them to their powers. Eventually, they will grow to take their ancestors' place and fill the vacated role. There will be other NPCs to fill the gods not chosen.<br /> <br /> In this way, it shouldn't be too big of an issue if the players don't know much about their parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T22:17:49-08:00","id":370759,"title":"","content":"I have run an Aesir and a Tuatha game as 'we're the only ones' (aka 'Tigger' games). Both went really well. The players told me each time that the focus made them feel more like they were in something special, as mixed pantheon games kind of make it all feel watered down a bit, so the single pantheon focus was well received.<br /> <br /> Can't help much with Egyptian or Chinese links though, sorry. But if you get something up and running, especially an Egyptian game, I'd love to hear about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:49:58-08:00","id":370957,"title":"","content":"Speaking of &quot;Tigger&quot; games, I tried a one-shot where everyone played scions of Odin. They were hidden away until after Ragnarok as some kind of insurance policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:37:34-08:00","id":372723,"title":"","content":"After delving into a few resource &amp; mythology sites (as well as looking at the in-game content), I have decided on a Pesedjet game.<br /> I found that <a href=\"http://www.ancientegyptonline.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ancientegyptonline.co.uk/</a> is rather helpful, as I tend to borrow liberally from existing myths and histories for plot points to my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T17:37:26-08:00","id":373122,"title":"","content":"I would love to know how it goes. Please keep us informed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T19:04:16-08:00","id":373213,"title":"","content":"Very nice concept, didn't run one or played myself but I would love to know how it goes too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4754-ironskin","name":"Ironskin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:03:54-08:00","id":413099,"title":"","content":"So I had my first character creation session last week. I decided to have the players design a normal human, then I would assign a deity based on back-story and skills (this may probably be easier once the new version comes out). After that, all players received a small box of trinkets, travel arraignments to Chicago, and a special event ticket for something held in the Field Museum's Egyptology exhibit.<br /> Here, the characters meet a varied band of people, each with a specific time to enter the exhibit. This group of players (I have a few others that couldn't make it) all enter at the same time, finding themselves whisked to the Egyptian afterlife, standing before the god Thoth. The characters are 'awakened' to their true selves and the trinkets are transformed into modern relics (a small one-on-one with each player to select their godly powers, relics, etc).<br /> Currently, I have:<br /> Autumn Lee (Re), Surf/paddle-board/yoga instructor from Pasadena.<br /> She has a spirit guide (seen as her old surf instructor form Oahu), Falcon bracelet (Animal purview), Tee shirt with sun motif (Sun purview, increased soak), and a surfboard made from a cedar plank of the Pharaoh Unis' barge (Water purview, summonable).<br /> <br /> Jack Allen (Ptah), Cosplay vlogger and Stargate aficionado from Chicago.<br /> He's got an Uraeus from a Pharoah's crown (Fire purview, works as a beefed-up Taser [player wanted a Zat]), clay tablet-themed iPad with prayer to Ptah on the back (Psychopomp purview), and a gold bracelet with a clear crystal scarab (Illusion purview, constant 'subtle knife' effect, improves soak of Body Armor knack and grants it a Stargate-like helm).<br /> <br /> Carrie Hallford (Sekhmet), Brewer, bow-hunter, and dryland musher (non-snow dogsledding using carts/bikes) from Traverse City.<br /> She has a summonable chariot (War purview), canopic jar featuring Duamutef (Animal purview, summons spirit-dog pack), pack of spirit-dogs (using Retainer rules from the Scion Overhaul, immortal with Epic Stamina), khopesh (Chaos purview, increased accuracy as sword longs for combat), sun-disk necklace (Sun purview), and an ancient bow (Fire purview, refills quiver for 1 legend).<br /> <br /> These three have been tasked with finding the &quot;Overseer of the Granaries of the Western Border&quot;*, given tickets, and ushered through a portal that places them at Union Station, there to board the 8:05pm train from Chicago to Memphis**.<br /> <br /> * A simple search will find this engraved on a block statue of Nedjem, formerly of Memphis, Egypt's Temple to Ptah and current centerpiece of the University of Memphis' selection of Egyptian artifacts.<br /> <br /> ** After a touch of research, I found that the 8:05pm Amtrack from Chicago, on 3 March 2015, boards just after Astronomical Twilight and arrives in Memphis, TN exactly at sunrise (6:27am). I could not pass this up, seeing as I could attack Re with the &quot;Scales of Apep&quot;, a cult I will be throwing at them in the early days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","user":"PHGraves","date":". 02-20-2015, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}